# Optional frontend build-time settings. Copy to frontend/.env to use them; none are
# required. These are read by Vite at build time, so re-run `npm run build` after changing.
#
# The routes map's tile source. The default is OpenStreetMap's public tiles, which need no
# key and no account -- but they are offered for low-volume personal use, and the map is off
# until you turn it on for that reason as much as for privacy (see ADR-0004).
#
# Point these at your own provider if you would rather not use OSM's, or want a style they
# don't offer. Two things to know if you do:
#
#   * Set the attribution as well. It is separate because it is not transferable: whatever
#     source you use has its own credit requirement, and OSM's applies only to OSM's tiles.
#     Overriding the URL alone ships no credit at all rather than the wrong one -- the OSM
#     default is deliberately not inherited onto another source's tiles.
#   * Dark mode inverts the tiles with a CSS filter (see RoutesMap.css), which assumes a
#     light source like the default. Point this at an already-dark style and dark mode will
#     invert it back to a light one.
#
# VITE_TILE_URL=https://tile.example.com/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?key=YOUR_KEY
# VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=&copy; <a href="https://example.com/">Example</a>
